.TH deductionguidesforstd::ranges::iota_view 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
deductionguidesforstd::ranges::iota_view \- deductionguidesforstd::ranges::iota_view

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <ranges>
template< class W, class Bound >

requires (!/*is-integer-like*/<W> ||
!/*is-integer-like*/<Bound> ||                                       \fI(since C++20)\fP
/*is-signed-integer-like*/<W> == /*is-signed-integer-like*/<Bound>)

iota_view( W, Bound ) -> iota_view<W, Bound>;

This deduction guide is provided for iota_view to allow deduction from an initial value
and a bounding value.

For the definitions of /*is-integer-like*/ and /*is-signed-integer-like*/, see
is-integer-like ﻿.

Note that the guide protects itself against bugs arising from sign mismatch, like
views::iota(0, v.size()), where 0 is signed and v.size() is unsigned.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <cassert>
#include <ranges>

int main()
{
    auto io = std::ranges::iota_view(1L, 7L); // deduces W and Bound as “long”
    assert(io.front() == 1L and io.back() == 6L);
}
